/*!
\page example_fetchcontent_integration FetchContent Integration Example

The FetchContent integration example demonstrates how to consume VanillaPDF using
CMake's FetchContent mechanism in real-world scenarios.

\section fetchcontent_features Features Demonstrated

- **Real GitHub Integration**: Fetches VanillaPDF from GitHub repository (not local source)
- **Cross-platform Testing**: Windows (vcpkg), Linux (apt), macOS (Homebrew) dependency strategies
- **CMake Test Integration**: Uses `add_test()` and `enable_testing()` for proper test execution
- **Dependency Management**: Shows both vcpkg and system package approaches
- **Actual PDF Creation**: Creates real PDF files and validates functionality

\section fetchcontent_usage Quick Usage

\code{.bash}
cd examples/fetchcontent-integration
cmake --preset windows-x64-debug  # or linux-x64-debug, macos-arm64-debug
cmake --build --preset windows-x64-debug
ctest --preset windows-x64-debug --output-on-failure
\endcode

\section fetchcontent_dependencies Dependency Management

The example demonstrates different dependency management strategies:

- **Windows**: Uses internal vcpkg for all dependencies
- **Linux**: Uses system packages (`apt-get install`) for faster builds
- **macOS**: Uses Homebrew packages (`brew install`) for faster builds

\section fetchcontent_ci Continuous Integration

This integration approach is continuously validated via automated CI workflows
across all supported platforms.

\note When using FetchContent, you are responsible for managing VanillaPDF's dependencies
through system package managers or other packaging systems.
*/

/*!
\page example_android_ndk_integration Android NDK Integration Example

The Android NDK integration example demonstrates how to cross-compile
vanillapdf for Android using CMake presets and vcpkg chainloading.

\section android_ndk_features Features Demonstrated

- **Android toolchain integration**: Uses Android NDK with CMake and Ninja
- **RID-compatible ABI mapping**: Presets map to `android-arm64`, `android-arm`, `android-x64`
- **vcpkg chainload flow**: Android NDK toolchain chained from vcpkg for dependency resolution
- **CI validation**: Build-only matrix validation for multiple Android ABIs

\section android_ndk_usage Quick Usage

\code{.bash}
export ANDROID_NDK_ROOT=/path/to/android/ndk
cd examples/android-ndk-integration
cmake --preset android-arm64-release
cmake --build --preset android-arm64-release
\endcode

\note This integration scenario validates cross-compilation and linking. The
produced binaries are not executed on the host CI machine.
*/

